# A denylist, not the previous "exclude everything (**), then re-include
# with ! patterns" approach: that relies on negation-after-blanket-exclude
# semantics that aren't interpreted identically across build engines. It
# worked under plain `docker build` but silently dropped the entire cmd/
# tree ("directory not found") under an OpenShift binary build (buildah) -
# found deploying cmd/extender. Test files and docs harmlessly riding along
# in the build context isn't worth that fragility.
.git
bin
cover.out
*.md
